THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The AGPL covers Sqemes' own code. Bundled and depended-upon third-party
components remain under their own licenses, which are unaffected by the change
above — including their attribution requirements, which continue to apply.

Dependencies include components under the Apache License 2.0; their own NOTICE
requirements are carried by this file.

**THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md** at the root of this distribution lists every npm
production dependency with its version, its licence, and the licence text as
published — grouped so identical texts appear once with the packages that ship
them. It also lists the pinned container images of the self-host bundle.

**sbom.json** is the same inventory in CycloneDX 1.5 form, for tooling.

Both are generated at release time from the dependency tree, not maintained by
hand: a notices file written once is accurate on that day and quietly wrong at
the next release, and a stale notice claims a completeness it no longer has.

For self-hosting convenience, this distribution bundles components of the Supabase
self-hosted stack under `selfhost/` — Postgres, GoTrue (Auth), PostgREST, Realtime,
Storage, Kong, edge-runtime, and Studio. Those components are the property of their
respective authors and are licensed under their own terms (Supabase's own components are
largely Apache-2.0; bundled databases/services carry PostgreSQL, MIT, and similar licenses).
Nothing here relicenses them.

`selfhost/docker-compose.yml`, `selfhost/volumes/`, and the Caddy TLS overlay
(`selfhost/docker-compose.caddy.yml`, `selfhost/volumes/proxy/caddy/`) are adapted from the
upstream `supabase/supabase` repository (Apache-2.0).

